    "lines": [
      {
        "scene": "hook",
        "text": "You think Buffett sells his big winners? Not this one. Here's why.",
        "start": 0.3,
        "seconds": 3.33,
        "window": 4.0,
        "fill": 0.833
      },
      {
        "scene": "promise",
        "text": "Berkshire finished buying these Coca-Cola shares decades ago, for $1.3B in total. Watch what that one purchase does.",
        "start": 4.3,
        "seconds": 7.85,
        "window": 8.53,
        "fill": 0.92
      },
      {
        "scene": "never",
        "text": "Never sold a single share? Then how does he get any money out of it?",
        "start": 12.83,
        "seconds": 3.29,
        "window": 3.7,
        "fill": 0.889
      },
      {
        "scene": "dividend",
        "text": "Coca-Cola pays its owners a slice of its profit every year. That slice is called a dividend.",
        "start": 16.53,
        "seconds": 5.15,
        "window": 5.8,
        "fill": 0.888
      },
      {
        "scene": "y1994",
        "text": "When the buying finished, the dividend was $205,479 a day. Worth waiting decades?",
        "start": 22.33,
        "seconds": 6.85,
        "window": 7.53,
        "fill": 0.91
      },
      {
        "scene": "why",
        "text": "Exactly. Why not sell and buy something faster?",
        "start": 29.87,
        "seconds": 2.22,
        "window": 2.73,
        "fill": 0.813
      },
      {
        "scene": "raise",
        "text": "Because Coca-Cola kept raising its dividend, year after year, while Berkshire's cost never moved.",
        "start": 32.6,
        "seconds": 5.14,
        "window": 5.83,
        "fill": 0.882
      },
      {
        "scene": "turn",
        "text": "And here's the twist. Decades later, the dividend was $704M a year. That's 54% of the whole price, paid back in one year.",
        "start": 38.43,
        "seconds": 8.71,
        "window": 9.37,
        "fill": 0.93
      },
      {
        "scene": "payoff",
        "text": "That's why Berkshire never sold. It keeps the tree and eats the fruit, about $1.9M a day by then.",
        "start": 47.8,
        "seconds": 6.46,
        "window": 7.1,
        "fill": 0.91
      },
      {
        "scene": "loop",
        "text": "That's one company's past, not a promise. But would you have kept it all those years, like Buffett?",
        "start": 54.9,
        "seconds": 4.94,
        "window": 5.53,
        "fill": 0.893
      }
    ]
